  "limits": [
    "The application NetworkSrf command remains unregistered. All three retained comparisons fail the 1e-6 returned-point target; the reference audit separately retains an exact incompatibility with simultaneous original-source preservation for one query. Saved SDK results supply comparisons only and never feed independent fitting.",
    "The original 4-to-64 curve, 2-to-32 family, degree-16, 128-control/source and 2048-total-input limits remain. Fitted polynomial families retain individual 128-control and total 2048-control limits. The first family reserves the opposite minimum basis; the second consumes the remainder. Uniform refinement has at most six seed levels and one final bounded refit. The order is greedy, not an optimal basis or performance claim.",
    "Curve-fit tolerance is one tenth of the smaller model tolerance. Sample distances measure every candidate point independently but are not continuous fit bounds. Restored contact constraints, complete fitted-curve admission and complete original-world image certificates remain independent gates. The original numerical, model and certificate work/bit/depth limits remain unchanged.",
    "Nearby contact searches use an exact translational sweep and certified control-hull separation but do not prove a global pair minimum, uniqueness, contact completeness, injectivity or surface topology. Unsupported or unproved cases reject. Complete natural endpoints are retained. If a UV fixed coordinate changes after pullback, its modified witness receives a fresh proof against the original surface and curve.",
    "All 20 retained complete original-image bounds satisfy 1e-6, and their UV definitions cover the original natural domains with the prescribed fixed coordinates. Seventy-five closest-point output comparisons are point-query diagnostics, not continuous surface separation bounds or qualified Rhino interior smoothing.",
    "Release native test linkage uses AddressSanitizer and frame pointers in SMLib, SM_API and the adapter, including the changed native fitting code. Rust and the debug oracle are not separately instrumented. Leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks remain disabled. No performance or boundary surface-continuity qualification is claimed."
  ],
